// Curated in-game essentials. Advanced options remain available in the INI.
// Group order: Attendance, Soundscape, Broadcast; toggles precede numeric controls.
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Enabled","Dynamic Attendance","Let fans arrive after kickoff, take halftime breaks and leave early. Turn this off to keep the game's normal crowd. Extra replays have their own switch.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"2020ModeEnabled","2020 Mode","Play with empty stands. Mute the crowd, bands, drums and PA announcer, but keep quiet individual voices and a more open stadium sound. Turn off to bring back normal attendance and sound.",0.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ArrivalsEnabled","Fans Arriving After Kickoff","Start with some fans still outside, then fill their seats during the first quarter. Turn off to start with the full expected crowd. This does not guarantee a sellout.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficEnabled","Beat the Traffic","Let fans leave sooner when the home team is far behind late in the game. With 12-minute quarters, this starts at 4:00 in Q4 when down 17+, or gently at 6:00 when down 28+.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"DynamicAwayCrowds","Visiting Fans","Give visiting fans their own sections and scattered seats. Their share depends on fanbase size, travel and rivalry. Choose before loading a fresh game; changing this does not recolor a crowd already loaded. Bands keep their uniforms.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"AttendanceProfile","Attendance Profile","Default keeps the normal mod balance. Fuller Crowds raises the expected peak by 8 percentage points in fresh regular-season Dynasty games and seats 7 more of every 100 expected fans at kickoff in those games. Existing caps and weather rules still apply; named showcase rivalries have their own starting ranges. Choose before loading a fresh game. Postseason crowds keep their own rules.",1,0,1,Kind::AttendanceProfile},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Profile","Fan Patience","Automatic follows the matchup and weather. Normal uses standard departures. Patient Fans makes people stay longer. Bad Weather makes people leave sooner. This does not change the starting crowd.",0,0,3,Kind::Profile},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"StartPercent","Ordinary Kickoff Crowd (%)","How much of the expected crowd starts in its seats. At 55, about 55 of every 100 expected fans are seated at kickoff. Smaller stadiums and special games can start fuller. Higher means more fans at kickoff. Applies to fresh games.",55.0,50.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolStartPercent","Late-Arriving Schools: Kickoff (%)","Kickoff crowd for UCLA, USC, Virginia, Miami (FL), Georgia Tech, Maryland and Utah. At 45, about 45 of every 100 expected fans start seated. Higher means more fans at kickoff. Night games and weather can change it. Applies to fresh games.",45.0,40.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameBonus","Big Game Kickoff Bonus (points)","Add up to 3 points to the seated share at kickoff. Big games mean two Top 25 teams, or rivals with either team Top 25 or both Top 50. Most regular games stay at 70% of expected fans or less; exceptional games can reach 80%.",3.0,0.0,3.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FinishPercentOfQuarter","When Arrivals Finish (% of Q1)","How far into Q1 ordinary schools finish filling up. At 50, fans finish halfway through the quarter. Higher means later arrivals. Big games, late-arriving schools and postseason games keep their own timing. Applies to fresh games.",50.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FormulaStrength","Fans Leaving Early (%)","How strongly the score, time and matchup make fans leave. 100 is normal, 50 is gentler and 200 is stronger. At 0, these departures stop. Halftime breaks and special late-game exits have their own settings.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeSeatBreakStrength","Halftime Seat Breaks (%)","How many fans temporarily leave their seats around halftime. 100 is normal; higher leaves more empty seats and lower leaves fewer. At 0, there are no temporary breaks. Fans who stay at the stadium return early in Q3.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Enabled","Crowd Sound Effects","Adjust crowd sound to the number of fans present and add reactions to plays. Turn off to keep the game's normal sound. Restart the game and MMC after changing this switch. 2020 Mode controls its own audio.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LayeredAtmosphereEnabled","Extra Crowd Energy","Add roars, buildup and stronger reactions when the game and crowd qualify. Sparse crowds can still get simple cheers or disappointment. Bigger effects and shake need enough seats filled. Turn off to stop these extra layers.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OpeningAtmosphere","Opening Atmosphere","Add intro and early-game energy. Qualifying big games and protected rivalries can get opening kickoff shake. If visitors open on offense, keep their first series loud until a first down or punt. Crowd fullness requirements still apply.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PlayCallAtmosphere","Play Selection Atmosphere","Build crowd noise while you choose a play and react to successful plays. Close games get extra energy in the last two minutes. Special cheers before the snap favor the home offense; at neutral stadiums either team can get them.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OvertimeAtmosphere","Overtime Atmosphere","Keep a qualifying overtime crowd lively between plays, kicks and two-point tries. Important results get a reaction, and crowd shake gets a small 10% lift. The crowd still needs enough seats filled.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"UpsetWatchAtmosphere","Upset Watch Sounds","Build excitement from Q2 onward when a home underdog threatens a Top 25 visitor. At least half the seats must be filled. At neutral sites, either underdog can qualify.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DuringPlayReactionsEnabled","Live Play Reactions","Let the crowd react during catches, runs, sacks, takeaways and returns. Bigger plays and larger crowds can use stronger sounds. Sparse crowds can still get sounds, but shake needs the normal crowd requirements.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SkillMoveReactions","Skill Move and Big Hit Reactions","React to successful moves and big hits. Trucks add a quick shake; hurdles and stiff arms add a gentler one. Spins, jukes and ordinary broken tackles add sound only. Big hits add truck-strength shake after a confirmed third- or fourth-down stop or any confirmed loss of yards.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PassFlightAnticipation","Buildup During Passes","Let the crowd build anticipation while a qualifying pass is in the air, then settle after the catch or incompletion. Does not add shake before the catch. Live Play Reactions must be on.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SituationalCrowdReactions","Cheers and Disappointment","Home and visiting fans react to good plays and mistakes. More supporters means a bigger response. Turn Away Team Reaction Shake off to keep visitor reactions sound-only. Neutral stadiums keep their usual shared-crowd balance.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"WinningEruptions","Major Celebrations","Use the biggest celebration for special moments, such as a very early touchdown, a late winning score, an overtime winner or a game-sealing takeaway. A long touchdown alone gets the normal touchdown celebration.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"CrowdMixStrengthPercent","Crowd Volume Adjustment (%)","How much the mod changes crowd volume for the fans present. 100 uses the normal mod mix. Lower stays closer to the game's normal volume; 0 keeps normal volume unless the stands are empty. Does not reduce the game's own excitement.",100,0,100,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PauseMenuFullness","Show Fullness in Pause Menu","Show the percentage of seats filled beside Resume in the pause menu. It updates when you open the menu. A dash means the crowd measurement is not ready yet.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CameraShake","Added Camera Shake","Allow camera shake added by this mod. Turn off to stop all of the mod's added shake. The game's Dynamic Camera Effects setting must also be on.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"WidePlayerCameraCompensation","Wide Player Camera Compensation","Camera zoom is balanced automatically. Turn On only if extremely wide RTG or player-lock views still feel weak: it allows extra correction on those views. Normal cameras usually do not need this. Added Camera Shake must be on.",0.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"ExtraReplaysEnabled","Additional Replays","Ask the game for more replays after plays. Turn off to stop these extra requests. The game can still show its own replays.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenBigPlays","Full-Screen Big Play Replays","Ask for full-screen replays after big plays. The game still chooses what it can show, and you can still skip replays normally. Additional Replays must be on.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"InsetAfterRoutinePlays","Small Replays During Play Selection","Allow small replay windows while you choose a play after ordinary runs and completions. Slow Sim has no play-selection screen, so it gets no added small window. Additional Replays must be on.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DefensiveHighlights","Defensive Play Replays","Allow extra replays after sacks and tackles for loss, along with interception and lost-fumble highlights. Additional Replays must be on.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"AwayTeamReactionShakeEnabled","Away Team Reaction Shake","Let visiting fans cause shake after their big plays and stops. More visiting fans means a stronger response. Off removes this shake but keeps crowd sounds. Normal atmosphere rules still apply. Neutral stadiums keep their separate control.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"NeutralSiteShakePercent","Neutral-Site Crowd Shake (%)","How strong the mod's crowd shake is for BOTH teams at a neutral stadium. 75 keeps the usual balance, 50 is half normal home-stadium strength and 100 is the same strength. 0 turns this crowd shake off. The crowd must qualify. Stadium cannon shake has its own setting.",75.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"OrdinaryShakeStrengthPercent","Normal Play Selection Shake (%)","Maximum shake during ordinary play selection. Higher is stronger; lower is gentler. At 0, this type is off. Buildup before a punt uses half this strength. A qualifying crowd is still needed.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CriticalShakeStrengthPercent","Important Down Shake (%)","Maximum pre-snap shake on qualifying third and fourth downs in close games. Higher is stronger; 0 turns this type off. Home-offense buildup is 25% gentler than when the home crowd is defending. A qualifying crowd is still needed.",10.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DuringPlayShakeStrengthPercent","Live Play Shake (%)","Strength of shake for gains, takeaways and important stops. Higher is stronger; 0 turns it off. Big events get more shake than routine ones. Kickoff returns build from25 to35 yards; punt returns from30 to40. Distinct crowd effects can add a small extra shake without doubling it. Picking up your own fumble adds no shake.",11.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeStrengthPercent","Touchdown Shake (%)","Shake level held after the first touchdown impact. Higher is stronger; lower is gentler. At 0, touchdown shake is off. An active run or catch reaction builds smoothly into the celebration.",16.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeStrengthPercent","Major Celebration Shake (%)","Shake level held after the first impact of a major celebration, such as a winning play. Higher is stronger; 0 turns this type off. An active play reaction builds smoothly into it.",22.5,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CannonShakeStrengthPercent","Stadium Cannon Shake (%)","Shake when a stadium cannon fires. Higher is stronger; 0 turns off its shake but keeps the cannon sound. Works even in sparse crowds. Added Camera Shake and the game's Dynamic Camera Effects must be on.",18.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"StandardCameraShakePercent","Standard Camera Shake (%)","How much added shake you get with the Standard camera. 100 is the recommended balance, 50 is half as strong and 200 is twice as strong. 0 turns added shake off for this camera. The crowd still needs to qualify for shake.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"ZoomCameraShakePercent","Zoom Camera Shake (%)","How much added shake you get with the Zoom camera. 100 is the recommended balance, 50 is half as strong and 200 is twice as strong. 0 turns added shake off for this camera. The crowd still needs to qualify for shake.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"All22CameraShakePercent","All-22 Camera Shake (%)","How much added shake you get with the All-22 camera. 100 is the recommended balance, 50 is half as strong and 200 is twice as strong. 0 turns added shake off for this camera. The crowd still needs to qualify for shake.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"WideCameraShakePercent","Wide Camera Shake (%)","How much added shake you get with the Wide camera. 100 is the recommended balance, 50 is half as strong and 200 is twice as strong. 0 turns added shake off for this camera. The crowd still needs to qualify for shake.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"BroadcastCameraShakePercent","Broadcast Camera Shake (%)","How much added shake you get with the Broadcast camera. 100 is the recommended balance, 50 is half as strong and 200 is twice as strong. 0 turns added shake off for this camera. The crowd still needs to qualify for shake.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},

// Appended to preserve all existing control IDs. Displayed with Attendance.
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"VisitorCrowdInfluencePercent","Visiting Fan Strength (%)","100 uses the normal travel model. Lower means fewer visitors; higher means more. Applies to new matchup plans. Saved crowds, neutral venues and protected fans stay intact.",100,0,200,Kind::Slider},
